{"text": " You can't fix your sleep at night, you fix it in the morning. There's one number that fixes most bad nights, and it isn't your bedtime. Say you wake up at 7 all week, then sleep in until 10 on the weekend. That's 3 hours. By Monday your body clock is in a different time zone, so you lie awake at midnight and drag yourself out of bed. The number is your wake-up time. Pick one you can keep 7 days a week, weekends 2, say 7.30. Step 2. When the alarm goes off, get daylight within 10 minutes. Open the curtains or have your coffee by the window. Step 3. Work backwards. If you need 8 hours, bedtime is 11.30, so set a second alarm at 11 to start winding down. But what about Saturday? You don't have to be strict, sleep in 1 hour max, 8.30 not 10. Keep that for a week and the jagged line goes flat. Monday stops feeling like jet lag and most nights you get sleepy around the same time. Here's your reset, same wake time, 7 days, daylight within 10 minutes, a wind-down alarm before bed, send this to the friend who sleeps until noon on Sundays. That's what Demure is for. You archive your dream today so you can see it tomorrow and break it down into small steps you can actually do. And follow because tomorrow's reel is what to do the morning after a bad night. If you want to try it out, I've put the link in the bio.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 2.5, "text": " You can't fix your sleep at night, you fix it in the morning.", "tokens": [50363, 921, 460, 470, 4259, 534, 3993, 379, 1755, 11, 345, 4259, 340, 287, 262, 3329, 13, 50503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11213724163995273, "compression_ratio": 1.6677966101694914, "no_speech_prob": 0.0007000796031206846, "words": [{"word": " You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.26, "probability": 0.8568582534790039}, {"word": " can't", "start": 0.26, "end": 0.56, "probability": 0.9757899343967438}, {"word": " fix", "start": 0.56, "end": 0.68, "probability": 0.9908044338226318}, {"word": " your", "start": 0.